{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018937-hierarchy-of-spirits","id":1018937,"title":"Hierarchy of spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-18T15:41:49-08:00","id":1018937,"title":"Hierarchy of spirits","content":"Anyone done anything with some sort of fleshed out hierarchy of spirits? Like for example the Lesser Key of Solomon or any other grimoire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T20:39:56-08:00","id":1019035,"title":"","content":"What would you be trying to do with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T14:16:51-08:00","id":1019420,"title":"","content":"Well, I was thinking about using it as setting background. Some sort of government paranormal taskforce investigating the spirit world. The spirit world have some sort of pantheon of a number of very powerful spirits as well as other minor spirits. Maybe I will add some cults who worship those major spirits and perhaps even some (dark) magicians who try to summon those entities for knowledge or power. I think I can do this with the Book of Spirits, Second Sight and the core book. Maybe a bit of Hunter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T15:47:43-08:00","id":1019460,"title":"","content":"Yep, those are the books to go for. Speaking of which, the local spirit court will have very different members depending on where it's set. An urban metropolis? A rural town? Or somewhere in the wilds, like a deep forest or a mountain range? This may also impact how the spirits act - city spirits have more emotion and concept spirits, who'd have trouble finding 'natural' instances of their favored Resonance, which means they have more incentive to meddle with the World of Flesh.<br /> <br /> It also occurs to me that the governmental TF in question is also very liekly to be backed up by a spirit or spirits - those of order, investigation, truth, and bureaucracy, and other related concepts. Whether they know it or not, and appreciate it or not.<br /> <br /> The Key of Solomon I'd implement more as a hierarchy of Goetia than spirits, or even an entire Temenos realm of Goetia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T01:04:56-08:00","id":1019652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jan Paparazzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018937-hierarchy-of-spirits#post1018937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone done anything with some sort of fleshed out hierarchy of spirits? Like for example the Lesser Key of Solomon or any other grimoire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Does not Mage and Werewolf give you basic idea of Spirits Hierarchy? It's there, literally, written simple hierarchy of spirits Ranks and what it mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T05:41:11-08:00","id":1021539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018937-hierarchy-of-spirits?p=1019652#post1019652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does not Mage and Werewolf give you basic idea of Spirits Hierarchy? It's there, literally, written simple hierarchy of spirits Ranks and what it mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't own mage or werewolf. I only got the book of spirits and that book divides spirits into categories like nature, artificial, conceptual and elemental spirits. But if there is a hierarchy, that would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T05:59:47-08:00","id":1021542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018937-hierarchy-of-spirits?p=1019460#post1019460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, those are the books to go for. Speaking of which, the local spirit court will have very different members depending on where it's set. An urban metropolis? A rural town? Or somewhere in the wilds, like a deep forest or a mountain range? This may also impact how the spirits act - city spirits have more emotion and concept spirits, who'd have trouble finding 'natural' instances of their favored Resonance, which means they have more incentive to meddle with the World of Flesh.<br /> <br /> It also occurs to me that the governmental TF in question is also very liekly to be backed up by a spirit or spirits - those of order, investigation, truth, and bureaucracy, and other related concepts. Whether they know it or not, and appreciate it or not.<br /> <br /> The Key of Solomon I'd implement more as a hierarchy of Goetia than spirits, or even an entire Temenos realm of Goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The location will be Chicago, because that city has a nic mix of rich and poor plus old industry and a financial center.<br /> 2. They will be followed by spirits. Interesting idea. Haven't thought of it. They will be aware of it, because some agents are mediums or psychics.<br /> 3. Don't know about Goetia. It's mage I guess, so I will do some research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T07:56:28-08:00","id":1021567,"title":"","content":"Best piece of advice I've ever been given with regard to spirits and building a spirit court: build it like a super exaggerated mob in a tv show, with high ranking spirits (like rank 4 or higher) being the well-rounded bosses who control the whole shebang and have seriously developed character, low ranking spirits (like rank 1 or 2) being super 1 dimensional foot-soldiers that don't matter too much. Like the Sopranos, Tony Soprano and his highest ranking mobsters have a lot of character and Tony himself is a rank 5 or 6 spirit in charge of an umia, a random soldier that does a protection racket and shows up in maybe 3 episodes, he's a rank 1 or 2 spirit that barely has enough self-awareness to actually survive and can be killed off pretty easily with no real plot issues going on unless something is actually focused around him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T04:45:25-08:00","id":1021939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jan Paparazzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018937-hierarchy-of-spirits?p=1021542#post1021542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. The location will be Chicago, because that city has a nic mix of rich and poor plus old industry and a financial center.<br /> 2. They will be followed by spirits. Interesting idea. Haven't thought of it. They will be aware of it, because some agents are mediums or psychics.<br /> 3. Don't know about Goetia. It's mage I guess, so I will do some research.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always glad to have inspired new thoughts. Perhaps the industry spirits and finance spirits are at war? Or maybe the finance spirits already won and are the ruling class, with industry spirits the oppressed and bullied ones who pay tithes of Essence to the former just to be allowed to survive.<br /> <br /> For the task force, if spirits are following them then that means they already are feeding on their Essence, and some probably have Fettered to them and are Urging them to act in a more Resonant way with them. Whether the team's psychics are seeing this as malevolent parasites or benevolent guardians heavily depends on context. We have an example hunter conspiracy, the Les Mysteres, who are duped into aiding the spirits feed on the mortal world without constraint.<br /> <br /> Goetia are probably not of concern in your story, it seems, but the basic stuff is that they're sorta like spirits but live in the Astral Space instead of the Shadow Realm. Ones in the Oneiroi, the individual souls of humans, are psychic splinter-personalities of that individual. Ones in the Temenos, the collective soul of humanity, are everything humans have thought or imagined of - deities, comic characters, famous celebrities as the masses imagine them to be, cultural archetypes and such. Ones in the Anima Mundi, the collective soul of the natural world, are... surprisingly close to spirits, but more like universal archetypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T04:46:44-08:00","id":1021940,"title":"","content":"Good idea. Pretty much a spirit sandbox. You know what? I just ditch the demons/Lesser Key of Solomon. And I replace it with a sandbox of spirits on one side and another sandbox of conspiracies, hedge magicians/witches, cults and psychics on the other side. I think it will turn out great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}